<===> README.md
# Empty output

Compilations without any CSS output. The C API didn't truncate an
existing output file in this case (the content of a previous run remained).
<===>
================================================================================
<===> definitions/input.scss
@mixin a {b: c}
@function d() {@return e}
<===> definitions/output.css

<===>
================================================================================
<===> empty_rule/input.scss
a {}
<===> empty_rule/output.css

<===>
================================================================================
<===> placeholder/input.scss
%a {b: c}
<===> placeholder/output.css

<===>
================================================================================
<===> silent_comment/input.scss
// nothing to output
<===> silent_comment/output.css

<===>
================================================================================
<===> use_without_css/input.scss
@use "x";
$b: x.$a;
<===> use_without_css/_x.scss
$a: 1;
<===> use_without_css/output.css

<===>
================================================================================
<===> variables/input.scss
$a: 1;
$b: $a + 1;
<===> variables/output.css

